\serialwrite sends bytes over the open serial port.
It takes one or more integers from 0 to 255, and sends
each one as a single byte:

\serialwrite 1 127 255

A serial port must be opened first with \openserialport,
otherwise you will get a "serial port is not open" error.
If an argument is not a number between 0 and 255, you will
get an error, but the bytes before it have already been
sent.

To send text instead of bytes, use \serialprint.
